Feature: Biosimilar Brand Sales Channel-wise Aggregation

  This feature calculates the total sales performance of biosimilar products (kanjinti, mvasi, riabni) across different channels (online, retail, mobile) using the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack table. The output is grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, and channel_name, and aggregates the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for sales data within 36 months from cdl_effective_date. Invalid or null cdl_effective_date records are logged with error messages.

  Background:
    Given the source table is "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack"
    And the brands to filter are "kanjinti", "mvasi", and "riabni"
    And the key attributes for grouping are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the sales metrics to aggregate are integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars
    And cdl_effective_date is in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And the time window is 36 months from cdl_effective_date (inclusive)
    And invalid or null cdl_effective_date records are excluded from aggregation and logged in "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log" with error_message

  Scenario Outline: Happy Path - Valid Sales Data Aggregation by Channel
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And cdl_effective_date is a valid date in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    When the data is filtered for brands "kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"
    And the time window filter is applied for 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    And the data is grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars is calculated for each group
    Then the output contains aggregated sales metrics for each group
    And the output format is a DataFrame with columns: brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, total_integrated_units, total_integrated_normalized_units, total_integrated_dollars

    Examples:
      | brand     | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp      | channel_name | competitor_flag |
      | kanjinti  | 2021-01-01         | 2022-06-15 10:00:00       | online       | false          |
      | mvasi     | 2022-03-15         | 2023-02-10 15:30:00       | retail       | true           |
      | riabni    | 2020-07-20         | 2022-05-05 09:45:00       | mobile       | false          |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Invalid or Null cdl_effective_date Handling
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And cdl_effective_date is <cdl_effective_date>
    When the data is processed for aggregation
    Then records with invalid or null cdl_effective_date are excluded from aggregation
    And these records are logged in "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log"
    And the error_message column contains "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | brand     | cdl_effective_date | error_message                                 |
      | kanjinti  | null               | "cdl_effective_date is null"                  |
      | mvasi     | "2022-15-40"       | "cdl_effective_date format invalid"           |
      | riabni    | "not_a_date"       | "cdl_effective_date format invalid"           |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Transaction Timestamp Outside 36-Month Window
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And cdl_effective_date is a valid date in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And transaction_timestamp is <transaction_timestamp>
    When the time window filter is applied for 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    Then records with transaction_timestamp outside the 36-month window are excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | brand     | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp      |
      | kanjinti  | 2021-01-01         | 2024-02-02 10:00:00       |
      | mvasi     | 2022-03-15         | 2026-04-01 15:30:00       |
      | riabni    | 2020-07-20         | 2024-08-01 09:45:00       |

  Scenario Outline: Data Validation - Channel Name and Competitor Flag
    Given the table contains records with channel_name = <channel_name>
    And competitor_flag is <competitor_flag>
    When the data is grouped by channel_name and competitor_flag
    Then the output contains correct grouping and aggregation for each channel and competitor_flag value

    Examples:
      | channel_name | competitor_flag |
      | online       | false          |
      | retail       | true           |
      | mobile       | false          |

  Scenario: Output Format and Destination
    Given the aggregation is complete
    When the output is generated
    Then the output is a DataFrame with columns: brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, total_integrated_units, total_integrated_normalized_units, total_integrated_dollars
    And the output can be optionally written to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_channelwise"

  Scenario Outline: Data-Driven Test - Multiple Brands and Channels
    Given the table contains records for brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And channel_name = <channel_name>
    And cdl_effective_date = <cdl_effective_date>
    And transaction_timestamp = <transaction_timestamp>
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output contains the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for each group

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel_name | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp      |
      | kanjinti  | online       | 2021-01-01         | 2022-01-01 10:00:00       |
      | mvasi     | retail       | 2022-03-15         | 2023-03-15 15:30:00       |
      | riabni    | mobile       | 2020-07-20         | 2021-07-20 09:45:00       |

  Scenario: Validation Rule - cdl_effective_date Format
    Given a record with cdl_effective_date
    When cdl_effective_date is not in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    Then the record is excluded from aggregation
    And logged with error_message "cdl_effective_date format invalid"

  Scenario: Validation Rule - Null cdl_effective_date
    Given a record with cdl_effective_date = null
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the record is excluded from aggregation
    And logged with error_message "cdl_effective_date is null"

  Scenario: Validation Rule - Null Sales Metrics
    Given a record with null integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, or integrated_dollars
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then null values are treated as zero in aggregation

  Scenario: Validation Rule - Grouping by All Key Attributes
    Given the aggregation logic is executed
    When grouping is performed
    Then the output is grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name

  Scenario: Error Path - No Matching Brands
    Given the table contains no records for brand_normalized_name in ("kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni")
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output is an empty DataFrame

  Scenario: Error Path - No Records Within 36-Month Window
    Given the table contains records for the specified brands
    And all transaction_timestamp values are outside the 36-month window from cdl_effective_date
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output is an empty DataFrame

